1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,800
A user represents a person who has access to Burp Suite Enterprise Edition via the web

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:14,920
interface or a system that is accessed via one of the APIs.

3
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:18,680
You can create new users directly in Burp Suite Enterprise Edition.

4
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:23,860
Alternatively, you can use SSO or SCIM to configure your users.

5
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:25,800
You can assign users to groups.

6
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:29,760
This allows you to grant permissions to users which are relevant to their roles.

7
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:33,560
Log in to Burp Suite Enterprise Edition as an administrator.

8
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:36,800
From the team menu, select all users.

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,320
To filter the list of users, click the filter buttons.

10
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:44,940
Before creating new users, we recommend connecting your SMTP server.

11
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:49,200
This makes it easier to invite new users to Burp Suite Enterprise Edition, reset passwords

12
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:51,240
and so on.

13
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:56,160
To create a new user in Burp Suite Enterprise Edition, log in to the Burp Suite Enterprise Edition

14
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:57,740
as an administrator.

15
00:00:57,740 --> 00:01:01,340
In the team menu, select Add a new user.

16
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:06,260
In the user credentials section, enter the details for the new user.

17
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:09,840
Under choose a login type, select Password.

18
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:14,580
To allow the user to login immediately, select Enabled.

19
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:18,200
Select the groups that you want the user to belong to.

20
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:22,020
When you've finished, scroll down and click Save.

21
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:24,980
The new user appears in the list of users.

22
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:29,860
If you have already connected your SMTP server, the user automatically receives an email invite

23
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:34,540
to complete the registration process and obtain their password.

24
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:38,700
If you haven't connected your SMTP server, you can copy the link when prompted and email

25
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:39,620
it to the user manually.

26
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:46,960
If you need to create a user to enable integration with other software, refer to Creating API Users.

27
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:49,560
You can edit most of the user details.

28
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:52,700
However, you can't change a user's login type.

29
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:56,280
To edit an existing user, log in to Burp Suite Enterprise.

30
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:58,140
Make sure you're an administrator.

31
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,620
From the team menu, select All Users.

32
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:03,440
Click the user in the list and edit their details.

33
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:07,560
When you've finished, scroll down and click Save.

34
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:12,440
If you have enabled SCIM integration, you need to manage any SCIM users and groups using your

35
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:15,220
identity provided administration console.

36
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:17,880
You can temporarily suspend the user.

37
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:22,060
You may want to do this if they are on extended leave, for example.

38
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:25,340
Ensure you're logged into Burp Suite Enterprise as an administrator.

39
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:28,060
From the team menu, select All Users.

40
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:29,500
Click the user in the list.

41
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:33,720
To temporarily suspend the user, deselect Enabled.

42
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:38,320
To delete a user, log in to Burp Suite Enterprise Edition, again as an administrator.

43
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:41,040
From the team menu, select All Users.

44
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:42,820
Find the user in the list.

45
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:46,800
In the right-hand column, click the Delete icon.

46
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,400
At the prompt, click Delete.

